course: dictionary
lesson: 12861
title: Enhanced: made better
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Enhanced is a word for something that has been made better. The -ed ending shows that the change has already happened. «The photo was enhanced to look brighter.» Someone changed the photo so it looks better, with more light and clearer colours.
explain: Enhance is the base word, and it changes its ending: enhance, enhances, enhancing, enhanced. «The new software enhances the pictures» means the software is making them better right now. To check your meaning, swap in better or stronger. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: Enhanced can also describe a thing, as an adjective. «The game came in an enhanced edition with extra levels.» An enhanced edition is a better version, with more added. In formal writing, enhanced can mean increased in amount or value, as in «the scheme enhanced pupils' attainment», which means it raised their results.
fact: Enhance means to make something better, stronger or more attractive.
fact: «Enhanced» is the past form of enhance, and it can also describe a thing that has been improved: an enhanced photo.
fact: «Enhanced» can mean given extra features, as in an enhanced version of a game.
fact: In formal writing, «enhanced» can mean increased in amount or value.
fact: Useful phrases: enhanced by, greatly enhanced, enhanced version, enhanced security.
exercise: «The old photo was enhanced on the computer, so the colours looked bright.» What does enhanced mean here? | *Made better, with brighter colours | Made smaller | Thrown away | Copied exactly with no changes
exercise: «A microscope gives an enhanced view of tiny things.» What does enhanced suggest? | Louder and faster | Smaller and dirtier | *Better and clearer than before | Hidden away from everyone
exercise: Lily says enhanced just means new. Why is she not quite right? | Enhanced means old and dusty | Enhanced means the same as broken | Enhanced means the same as new, so there is no difference at all | *Enhanced means made better or stronger, not just new
test: «The game has an enhanced version with better graphics.» What is an enhanced version? | *A version that has been made better | A version that has been lost | A copy with no changes at all | A version with fewer features
test: Which phrase means security that has been made stronger? | Cold weather | Sunny day | Lost property | *Enhanced security
exam: «The scheme greatly enhanced pupils' attainment.» In this sentence, enhanced most nearly means | Ended | *Improved or increased | Argued about | Forgotten
